sec.p:
With these formulations in place, we can write down the equation of state describing the elastic forces (F) and torques (i.e., moments, M) on a point s on the filament at time t for a given filament configuration as;

(1)

M(s,t)=Kb(κ1d1+κ2d2)+KtΩd3,F(s,t)=b1d1⋅∂sX+b2d2⋅∂sX+b3(d3⋅∂sX−1).
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{array}{r} \mathbf{M}(s, t)=K_{b}\left(\kappa_{1} \mathbf{d}_{1}+\kappa_{2} \mathbf{d}_{2}\right)+K_{t} \Omega \mathbf{d}_{3}, \\ \mathbf{F}(s, t)=b_{1} \mathbf{d}_{1} \cdot \partial_{s} \mathbf{X}+b_{2} \mathbf{d}_{2} \cdot \partial_{s} \mathbf{X}+b_{3}\left(\mathbf{d}_{3} \cdot \partial_{s} \mathbf{X}-1\right) . \tag{1} \end{array}$$\end{document}



where we introduced the twist coefficient, Kt, and the bending coefficient, Kb, describing the resistance of the filament to twisting and bending, respectively, and b3 and b1, b2 describe its resistance to stretch and shear, with bi > Kb, Kt.

With the above definitions in place, we can write the force balance on a point s on the filament at time t. To do so, we use a coupled system of equations where the elastic forces and torques generated by the bending and twisting of the filament are transmitted to the viscous fluid. The rod experiences the elastic forces and torques from eq. (1), active force and torque densities fglide, nglide from gliding, viscous forces and torques from the fluid fv, nv, and steric interactions with the surface fste. The force and moment balance is;

(2)

∂sF(s,t)+fv(s,t)+fglide(s,t)+fadh(s,t)+fste(s,t)=0,∂sM(s,t)+d3×F(s,t)+nv(s,t)+nglide(s,t)=0.
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{align*} \partial_{s} \mathbf{F}(s, t)+\mathbf{f}_{v}(s, t)+\mathbf{f}_{\text {glide }}(s, t)+\mathbf{f}_{\text {adh }}(s, t)+\mathbf{f}_{\text {ste }}(s, t) & =\mathbf{0}, \\ \partial_{s} \mathbf{M}(s, t)+\mathbf{d}_{3} \times \mathbf{F}(s, t)+\mathbf{n}_{v}(s, t)+\mathbf{n}_{\text {glide }}(s, t) & =\mathbf{0} . \tag{2} \end{align*}$$\end{document}
